Article 2 (Approval and Reporting of Important Policy Matters, etc.) (1) The Commissioner of the Korea Coast Guard (hereinafter referred to as the "Commissioner") shall obtain prior approval from the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries (hereinafter referred to as the "Minister") concerning any of the following matters:
1. Formulation of or amendment to a master plan for the maritime police field requiring enactment or amendment of statutes or regulations;
2. Formulation of or amendment to major plans concerning international cooperation;
3. Accession to international organizations and conclusion of international agreements.
(2) The Commissioner shall report in advance to the Minister concerning the following matters:
1. Matters to be placed on the agenda of the State Council;
2. The Commissioner's attendance at international conferences or official travel abroad.
(3) The Commissioner shall report to the Minister concerning any of the following matters:
1. Plans for carrying out instructions from the President, the Prime Minister, and the Minister, and the results thereof;
2. Results of implementing major policies and plans;
3. Important matters among materials reported or submitted to the President, the Prime Minister, their directly affiliated agencies, the National Assembly, the Board of Audit and Inspection, or other relevant bodies;
4. Matters related to major policies among audit results and requests for disciplinary or corrective action from the Board of Audit and Inspection;
5. Other matters that the Minister requests as necessary for exercising statutory authority and performing official duties.
